WEBVTT

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:05.490
<i>Karoku.</i>

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.830
<i>Nai. Come here.</i>

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.170
<i>Karoku.</i>

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.050
<i>If I were...</i>

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.720
<i>Karoku.</i>

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:36.020
<i>Where have you gone?</i>

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.970
Are you nervous?

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.070
You are pushing my stomach.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.580
Makes me nauseous.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.160
You're heavy.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.580
What do you mean I make you nauseous.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.710
These are Karoku's.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.680
The Circus I.D.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:51.470
Did they... find us?

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.120
What was that? Intruders?

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:11.910
Check it!

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:49.740
KARNEVAL

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.740
Darn it. There's only junk.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.240
Rainbow Colored Flower Fuse
Score 1
Darn it. There's only junk.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.410
Excuse me...

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.750
What?

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:05.250
Ah, are you going to escape?

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.010
What?

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.260
I want to escape, too.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:12.470
But...

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:19.770
You have something interesting.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.520
I might be able to take you out of here.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.270
Really?

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.320
But, only on one condition.

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:30.780
That bracelet, give it to me.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.780
Sure, but this is Karoku's.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.030
If Karoku says you can have it, it's okay with me.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.250
It's a deal.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.170
Damn it. She's back.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.760
Are you with Circus?

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:54.680
You can't be...

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:59.350
You're just a little thief, aren't you?

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:01.680
So what?

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:06.560
It's fine. Run away.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.860
What?

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:12.070
Let's play tag.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:20.780
But I will catch you soon!

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:20.790
What are you?
But I will catch you soon!

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:21.740
What are you?

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.930
Hey, come on!

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.530
Welcome back, Tsukumo-chan.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:02.330
I was having a cup of tea while I was waiting for you.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.830
Hey, we're in public.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.210
Yes, yes, don't worry.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.750
I am concealing my presence.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.300
No one noticed me, right?

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.130
Jeez...

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:16.760
Anyway, report what Mine, the proprietor of the Karasuna, has to say.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.760
As we expected.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.390
We will leave right away.

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:30.610
Damn it.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:32.070
Come out!

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:35.950
Move one step, the wings are torn...

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:37.490
Move two steps, the innards are gone...

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:38.700
Mine-sama!
Move two steps, the innards are gone...

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:39.370
Move two steps, the innards are gone...

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.330
I tracked down the intruders here!
Move two steps, the innards are gone...

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:45.210
Move three steps, you become a feast for death.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.460
Mine-sama?
Move three steps, you become a feast for death.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.170
Move three steps, you become a feast for death.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.810
Well, that didn't work out like I expected.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.860
If I don't eat enough, I won't be able to move <i>fast</i> enough.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.230
<i>What is... she?
If I don't eat enough, I won't be able to move fast</i> enough.

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:13.650
<i>What is... she?</i>

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:24.910
Yes, that's right.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:25.500
Got it.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.500
Check–

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:34.130
Didn't I say a tag, not hide-and-seek?

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:39.800
You have to run farther.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.210
U-Um...

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.630
what happened to her?

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:25.350
<i>I only ever have three choices.</i>

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:31.270
<i>Enemy, nobody, or prey.</i>

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:32.980
Well..

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.320
<i>This one is...</i>

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:57.330
I am Gareki, and you?

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:58.460
Nai.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:04.470
Palnedo, CEO of Gardo Corporation, how do you like to ride in the cattle-class?

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.760
It must be very different from first-class.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.140
What are you going to do with me?

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.650
It hurts.

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:20.740
That damn brat...

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.870
What?

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:31.410
Whoa, I didn't know you were here.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.540
What a surprise.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.170
It's kind of a mess...

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:37.040
You could have lived longer if you had stuck with collecting money.
It's kind of a mess...

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.040
You could have lived longer if you had stuck with collecting money.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:44.010
Hey, don't fall behind!

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.940
Smoke?

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:06.740
Oh well, another dead end...

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:10.580
They got away again.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.500
This woman, Mine, was the one we had the evidence on.

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:18.750
So close...

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.550
What's wrong?

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:29.260
Yes, I regret to say they made the first move here.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:32.260
Train jacking?

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.730
The Security Force is already on the move?

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.270
All right, I understand.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.810
Security Force?

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.350
They're already making a move?

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:45.770
Dammit!

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:53.530
What about over there?

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.250
This is not good.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.910
Leaving town seems to be the only option.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:08.210
But this town's exit gates must be closed by now.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:22.430
Listen,

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.360
when I give the signal, you jump off.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:27.070
Y-Yes.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:35.750
Let's go!

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:14.230
Karoku...

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:28.920
This can't be real.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:32.080
Why was the proprietor of the Karasuna such a monster...

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:32.550
Um...
Why was the proprietor of the Karasuna such a monster...

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:32.790
Um...

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:37.930
Thank you for helping me.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:46.650
Why were you in captivity?

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:50.450
Well, I was looking for Karoku...

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.320
What does this Karoku have to do with you?

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:57.450
Karoku was always with me.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.080
But...

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.030
Ah?

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.290
Karoku didn't come home for a long time so I got lonely.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.090
So I went to look for him.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:13.510
I saw many red puddles, large and small, leading toward the ocean.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:16.600
Then, I found this there.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.770
You talk oddly...

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:24.600
Rather, that was blood, wasn't it?

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:29.190
He got involved in some mess and got abducted, didn't he?

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:34.530
If not, he was dragged to the ocean and thrown in.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:40.740
<i>Come to think of it, she said this bracelet was a Circus I.D.</i>

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:46.250
<i>From his story, I can't think of Karoku as a member of Circus.</i>

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:50.340
<i>I can't work in Karasuna for a little while.</i>

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:54.130
<i>Even if I don't get that bracelet, I can probably get some kind of reward.</i>

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:56.420
<i>I won't lose anything.</i>

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:07.180
<i>I wonder how long it's been since I last saw Karoku.</i>

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.850
<i>I want to eat with him.</i>

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.640
<i>My body hurts in many places.</i>

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:16.030
<i>Karoku.</i>

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.910
Hey you, what are you doing?

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.040
I heard a strange sound.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.710
Sound?

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:29.040
I don't hear anything strange.

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.340
Now that you mention it, there are no passengers...

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:38.470
Gareki, where are you going?

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:40.680
There is something strange going on.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:43.100
I'm going to check it out.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:45.600
You will be in the way so stay here...

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.110
Gareki.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:04.120
I never thought the hijackers would have a kid as their lookout.
Gareki.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.620
I never thought the hijackers would have a kid as their lookout.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:06.650
In the back, there was a noise.
I never thought the hijackers would have a kid as their lookout.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:07.620
In the back, there was a noise.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:08.370
Who's there?

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.080
Who are you guys?

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.210
What are you doing here?

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:18.590
If you two are not in their group, you should have told me.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:19.300
Answer me!

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:19.840
Come again?

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:20.970
Dammit.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.210
Tsukumo, let's go.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:47.870
Yes, sir.

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:53.920
Darn it.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:56.630
Gareki.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.880
Well, we seem to be caught up in something annoying.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:04.090
Even so, who was that guy in black?

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:07.390
That sound from before.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:08.380
What?

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:10.900
Up front.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:12.650
Hey!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:17.320
Listen, if you move an inch,

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.650
we will shoot them.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:31.580
Why can't we beat them?

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:35.500
By the looks of it, they are ordinary citizens.

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:38.010
It will cause trouble if we step out of our jurisdiction.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:42.680
You ruined our lives!

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:49.430
In order for the company to survive, laying off workers was unavoidable.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.190
You say that is evil,

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:58.070
but you are doing even worse by getting my innocent granddaughter involved.

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.570
Shut up! Shut up!

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.200
Here!

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:04.450
Who are you guys?

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:05.490
Where did you come from?

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:06.030
Crap!

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:10.990
Come out you brats!

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:13.830
Isn't that enough?

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.540
You'd better stop it.

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:22.220
It is only a sad foolish act if you are causing this destruction in order to release your frustrations.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:23.470
Shut up!

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:52.910
The bombs we set in each carriage will start to explode one by one...

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:57.420
If you stop the train, all of them will explode at once...

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.250
Are you serious?

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:03.420
We were planning on taking Palnedo with us from the beginning.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:08.050
I am sorry to say, you will all be coming with us.

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:13.060
Tsukumo, take these two somewhere safe.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:15.400
I will take care of the bombs.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:16.690
Yes.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:19.310
Well, who are you two?

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:26.070
I am the Second Ship Captain, Hirato, of the National Defense Organization, Circus.

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:30.330
I am the Second Ship fighter, Tsukumo.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:34.710
There is a girl like you in Circus?

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:36.710
Yes.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.220
<i>What?</i>

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:47.800
<i>He reacted before the explosion.</i>

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:49.180
Sound.

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:49.970
Sound?

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:54.050
There is electrical interference.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:54.970
Tsukumo,

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:59.480
the worst case scenario is to evacuate everyone and derail the train.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:00.400
There will be residential areas from here on.

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.190
<i>Electrical interference?
There will be residential areas from here on.</i>

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:03.980
<i>It can't be.
There will be residential areas from here on.</i>

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:08.240
We have to make sure not to slow down.
<i>But, it's too late to think after your dead.</i>

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.160
Hey, four-eyed shithead!

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.370
Four-eyed shithead?

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.120
Get over here.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.870
There's still a chance.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:19.420
Come here!

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:24.630
Nai, where is that sound coming from?

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:32.880
Here.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.890
Stand back.

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:39.640
There it is!

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:43.020
But this isn't a bomb.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:44.820
Just an electric jammer.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:46.530
There are a bunch of fakes.

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:49.650
The base is made by ST, electrically ignited, the route to ignite the explosion is this.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:53.030
And this is the electric detection device.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:58.790
This one is not connected with radio wave induction.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:02.660
This thing hasn't synchronized with the radio transmitter yet.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:11.470
The point is, we have to separate the back of the train before the radio waves reach it.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.510
That answer is worth trusting.

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:16.100
Stand back, both of you.

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:26.110
<i>Vakuum</i>!

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:54.800
Gareki, where are you going?

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.980
I am taking off before the Security Force finds me.

00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:04.270
Um... Gareki.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:05.230
What?

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:08.860
Thank you.

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:09.780
Come again?

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:12.530
You saved me again.

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:18.030
Is it all right?

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:20.040
The bracelet that boy had...

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:21.710
You recognized it, didn't you?

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:22.790
Of course.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.920
But now...

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:33.800
Excuse me.

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:37.800
Can you spare me a few minutes?

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:42.430
I do not wish to refuse to cooperate with the investigation,

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:46.190
but I have been feeling a pain in my chest for some time now.

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:47.440
Well...

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:50.490
I am quite old as you can see.

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:55.070
And my doctor is here to see me. I am sorry but I will have to excuse myself.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:59.320
Then, we'll talk some other time.

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:08.160
I took care of the Karasuna incident.

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.670
Well, you look exhausted.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:17.090
I let myself be captured on purpose to see how effective Circus is.

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:20.600
They are as I expected.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:23.980
Please do not play around too much.

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:28.100
If there is a need, we will always take action.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:31.520
Speaking of which, I saw someone interesting.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:35.240
He seems to have some unique ears.

00:21:35.240 --> 00:21:37.740
He looks little bit like "him."

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:39.830
Can you capture him?

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:44.370
Hirato of Circus seems to be interested in him too.

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:53.960
It's done!

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:27.970
Tsukumo

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:29.510
These, snacks–they seem strange?

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:31.970
I bought them at a café in Karasuna.

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:34.770
Muffins, scones, short breads.

00:23:34.770 --> 00:23:36.060
There are so many.

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:37.400
These are souvenirs for Yogi.

00:23:37.400 --> 00:23:39.110
Treating him like a child–?
